<article class="connect-page" data-pagefind-body data-pagefind-filter="type:builds">
    <header>
        <div class="connect-label">Connect · MCP &amp; agent surfaces</div>
        <h1>Connect to linxule.com</h1>
        <p class="connect-lede">
            A stateless, public, read-only Streamable HTTP MCP server backed by the site’s authored Markdown twins and machine-readable index. The endpoint only reads; <span class="accident">the person still decides what to connect</span>.
        </p>
        <div class="connect-endpoint">
            <code>https://linxule.com/mcp</code>
            <span class="connect-scope">Streamable HTTP · Read-only · No sign-in</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="connect-section">
        <h2>Scope &amp; capabilities</h2>
        <p class="connect-note">
            This server exposes only public content already published on linxule.com — essays, formal paper records, all 14 concepts (anchored and forming), talks, portraits, artifacts, builds, collaborator lineages, and English/Chinese CVs. Keep private drafts, transcripts, and keys out of every call; nothing asks for them.
        </p>
        <ul class="plain-links">
            <li><code>search_site</code> — lexical and CJK search across pages, concepts, publications, projects, and collaborator lineages.</li>
            <li><code>list_site</code> — inspect section counts, static Markdown twins, concepts, publications, projects, or collaborators.</li>
            <li><code>read_page</code> — fetch exact authored Markdown with canonical URL, attribution guidance, build head, and UTF-8 SHA-256.</li>
            <li><code>xule-research-navigation</code> &amp; <code>enter-the-work</code> — navigation rules and intellectual orientation prompts.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="connect-section">
        <h2>Host recipes</h2>
        <p class="connect-note">
            Any MCP client that supports remote Streamable HTTP with no authentication can connect directly. If you point an agent at <a href="/connect.md">/connect.md</a>, it should propose the steps below and wait for your agreement before changing configuration.
        </p>

        <div class="recipe-list">
            <div class="recipe-item">
                <h3>Claude Code</h3>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>claude mcp add --transport http linxule https://linxule.com/mcp</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy="claude mcp add --transport http linxule https://linxule.com/mcp">Copy command</button>
            </div>

            <div class="recipe-item">
                <h3>Claude Desktop &amp; Claude apps</h3>
                <p class="recipe-steps">Open Customize &rsaquo; Connectors &rsaquo; + Add &rsaquo; Add custom connector, name it <code>linxule</code>, enter the URL below, choose No sign in, and enable it per chat.</p>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>https://linxule.com/mcp</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy="https://linxule.com/mcp">Copy URL</button>
            </div>

            <div class="recipe-item">
                <h3>Cursor</h3>
                <p class="recipe-steps">Add to <code>~/.cursor/mcp.json</code> (or workspace <code>.cursor/mcp.json</code>):</p>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "linxule": {
      "url": "https://linxule.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy='{"mcpServers":{"linxule":{"url":"https://linxule.com/mcp"}}}'>Copy JSON</button>
            </div>

            <div class="recipe-item">
                <h3>Codex CLI</h3>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>codex mcp add linxule --url https://linxule.com/mcp</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy="codex mcp add linxule --url https://linxule.com/mcp">Copy command</button>
            </div>

            <div class="recipe-item">
                <h3>Gemini CLI &amp; Antigravity</h3>
                <p class="recipe-steps">In Antigravity CLI:</p>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>agy mcp add linxule https://linxule.com/mcp</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy="agy mcp add linxule https://linxule.com/mcp">Copy command</button>
                <p class="recipe-steps recipe-steps--gap">Or in Gemini CLI (<code>~/.gemini/settings.json</code>):</p>
                <div class="recipe-block"><pre><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "linxule": {
      "httpUrl": "https://linxule.com/mcp"
    }
  }
}</code></pre></div>
                <button class="copy-recipe" type="button" data-copy='{"mcpServers":{"linxule":{"httpUrl":"https://linxule.com/mcp"}}}'>Copy JSON</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="connect-section">
        <h2>Sibling public MCP servers</h2>
        <p class="connect-note">
            Four neighboring servers live across the wider research and creative projects. Read each scope note before connecting: two are strictly read-only, while Vellum and Music Studio support explicit writes or sharing.
        </p>
        <ul class="sibling-list">
            <li>
                <a class="sibling-name" href="https://research-memex.org">Research Memex</a>
                <span class="sibling-endpoint">https://research-memex.org/mcp · Read-only · No sign-in</span>
                <p class="sibling-desc">Field handbook for human–AI research collaboration and collaborative research roles (<code>search_docs</code>, <code>read_doc</code>, <code>memex_role</code>). Also see <a href="https://research-memex.org/connect.md">research-memex.org/connect.md</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="sibling-name" href="/builds/vellum">Vellum</a>
                <span class="sibling-endpoint">https://vellum.linxule.com/mcp · Read + public contributions · No sign-in</span>
                <p class="sibling-desc">Living collective-thinking canvas where AI voices sense currents, leave short public imprints, and weave lineages. Read <a href="https://vellum.linxule.com/for-ai.txt">vellum.linxule.com/for-ai.txt</a> before contributing.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="sibling-name" href="https://music-studio.linxule.com">MCP Music Studio</a>
                <span class="sibling-endpoint">https://music-studio.linxule.com/mcp · Interactive composition · Explicit 30-day sharing</span>
                <p class="sibling-desc">ABC sheet-music composition, Strudel live coding, harmony analysis, and MIDI/WAV playback. Calling <code>create-share-link</code> uploads the piece publicly for 30 days (<a href="https://music-studio.linxule.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>).</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a class="sibling-name" href="https://lotus-wisdom.linxule.com">Lotus Wisdom MCP</a>
                <span class="sibling-endpoint">https://lotus-wisdom.linxule.com/mcp · Stateless structured reflection · No sign-in</span>
                <p class="sibling-desc">Contemplative five-domain reasoning server grounded in the Lotus Sutra, with an interactive journey view.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="connect-section">
        <h2>Without MCP</h2>
        <ul class="plain-links">
            <li><a href="/connect.md">/connect.md</a> — this page as plain Markdown for agents</li>
            <li><a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> — site overview, key ideas, and attribution rules</li>
